                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1629-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>AKG Acoustics C451 Anniversary</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Cardioid Pencil Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>AKG&#8217;s &#8220;65th Anniversary&#8221; edition of the C451B is a cosmetic upgrade to the C 451 B. </p><p>Both mics are electret pencil mics designed to recreate the sound of the discontinued C451 EB with CK1 cardioid capsule. Onboard switches allow selection of a 3-way high-pass filter (flat, 75Hz, 150Hz) and 3-way pad (0dB, -10dB, -20dB).</p><p>The Anniversary Edition is finished in a semi-gloss black finish called &#8220;Titan.&#8221; It ships with the SA60 stand adaptor and W90 foam windscreen, in commemorative packaging.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/AKG-Acoustics/C451-Anniversary">AKG Acoustics C451-Anniversary</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2012.</p>
